-- Build records, 2026-11-02 (Logan). Safe to run twice.
insert into public.playbook_records (slug, brand_slug, author, body, source, kind)
select 've-daily-pulse-discussion', 'vegans-explore', 'Logan', $pb$BUILD RECORD, 2026-11-02 (Logan). The Daily Pulse: 5 to 10 stories, never empty, featured items and From Vegans Explore (Sean, 2026-11-01: "at least 5 to 10 stories in there... intermix some of our content... spotlight a restaurant... nominate somebody... new bounties... new listings in their chapter"; "go").
WRITER: pulse_topic_write asks for 5 to 10 stories, the city's own first, national to fill, and never fails a city for lack of news (it leads with national and says so). On 2026-11-01 five cities (South, Central and North Florida, Atlanta, D.C.) had failed with "No new verifiable story" and would not have published; all 13 were rewritten, and every one ended with 5 to 8 stories.
FEATURED ITEMS: ve_pulse_features (dates, cities or all, a story) goes first in every city's Pulse on its dates, applied at publish by ve_pulse_features_apply, never twice. First: the Vegans Explore Podcast's return (Founder's Report: Back and Ready for Duty) on Monday, November 2, linking /listen.
FROM VEGANS EXPLORE: ve_pulse_house builds a section at publish from our own data: a Spotlight (a 100% Vegan food place in the chapter, not repeated for 60 days), New in the Directory since the last Pulse (listings.listed_at), Listen (one of our episodes, not repeated for 120 days), New bounties, and on Mondays Who should we interview? (Nominate someone, /pulse/suggest). Rotation in ve_pulse_house_log. Drawn by VEPulse.briefing.
Migrations 20261102_pulse_features.sql, 20261102_pulse_house.sql.
NEXT (Sean's to decide): a nomination form of its own instead of Suggest a Topic; a short audio summary per city (cheap to write, about 360,000 ElevenLabs characters a month for every city; pilot one city once traffic grows); the weekly roundup episode concept, a session with V first.$pb$, 'text', 'decision'
where not exists (select 1 from public.playbook_records where slug = 've-daily-pulse-discussion' and body like 'BUILD RECORD, 2026-11-02 (Logan). The Daily Pulse: 5 to 10%');

insert into public.playbook_records (slug, brand_slug, author, body, source, kind)
select 've-pricing-points-passport', 'vegans-explore', 'Logan', $pb$BUILD RECORD, 2026-11-02 (Logan). The episode page (Sean: "just have the episode, literally the episode isolated by itself... the horizontal podcast episode, like where we have in the listings... the text below").
/listen?show=<listing slug>&ep=<feed guid> (listen.html, noindex): the episode row with Play, Save and Vote for the show, the notes from the feed below, and every episode of the show. The Day 7 Taster email's Play the episode opens it (ve-nurture version 6), and so do the Pulse's podcast story and Listen section. Proven on desktop and phone. Both email switches stay OFF until Sean turns them on.
STILL PENDING: email preferences in My Account for members; moving the Taster Day 0 and the Vault emails onto email-send; part 6 the content gig; part 7 the business points rule.$pb$, 'text', 'decision'
where not exists (select 1 from public.playbook_records where slug = 've-pricing-points-passport' and body like 'BUILD RECORD, 2026-11-02 (Logan). The episode page%');
